This License is a modified version of the Mozilla Public License, Version 2.0
("MPL 2.0"), created and used under Section 10.3 of the MPL 2.0, which permits
anyone to make and use a renamed, modified version of that license.

  THIS LICENSE IS NOT THE MOZILLA PUBLIC LICENSE. The Mozilla Foundation is not
  the steward of this License, was not involved in its creation, and does not
  endorse it. Beamstack is the steward of this License.

This License is NOT an "open source" license as defined by the Open Source
Initiative, and is NOT a "free software" license as defined by the Free Software
Foundation, because it withholds the right to sell the software, requires
attribution in a user interface, and - for Covered Software that carries the
Exhibit C notice - requires source disclosure for network deployments. It is a
"source-available" license.

It differs from the MPL 2.0 in the following material respects:

  1. Section 1 adds definitions 1.15 through 1.20 ("Sell", "Deploy",
     "Attribution Mark", "Notice Files", "Network Deployment", "Corresponding
     Source").
  2. Section 3.6 ("No Sale") withholds the right to Sell the Covered Software or
     to provide, for a fee, a product or service whose value derives
     substantially from it. Internal use - including use to produce paid
     deliverables for clients - is not restricted.
  3. Section 3.7 ("Attribution") requires visible credit to Beamstack
     ("Powered by Beamstack" or the Beamstack logo) in the user interface,
     documentation, and package metadata of works built on the Covered
     Software, and requires the Notice Files to be kept intact.
  4. Section 3.8 ("Network Use") - a condition ONLY for Covered Software to
     which the initial Contributor has attached the Exhibit C notice - requires
     that, if You deploy a modified version so that others interact with it over
     a network (expressly including in-browser or other client-side execution,
     and access through an API or an automated agent), You offer those users the
     Corresponding Source of Your version, at no charge, under this License. If
     Exhibit C is not attached, Section 3.8 has no effect.
  5. Section 2.7 adds Sections 3.6 and 3.7 to the conditions of the grant, and
     Section 3.8 for Exhibit C software.
  6. The MPL 2.0 "Secondary License" / GPL-compatibility machinery is removed:
     definitions 1.5 and 1.12, the second sentence onward of Section 3.3,
     Section 10.4, and Exhibit B are struck. Covered Software may not be
     re-distributed under the GNU GPL, LGPL, or AGPL.
  7. Sections 2.3, 2.4, 10.1, and 10.3, and Exhibit A, are adjusted to name
     Beamstack and to reflect the changes above.

CHANGES IN VERSION 1.1 (from version 1.0): added the notice-activated Section
3.8 ("Network Use"), definitions 1.19-1.20, and Exhibit C. Version 1.0 had no
network-use condition. Covered Software that does not carry the Exhibit C notice
behaves identically under version 1.1 and version 1.0.

SPDX identifier: use "LicenseRef-BCL-1.1". Covered Software that attaches the
Exhibit C notice (Network Use active) should be identified as
"LicenseRef-BCL-1.1-Network" so the difference is visible to tooling and to
readers.

Everything else tracks the MPL 2.0. A plain-language summary of what you may and
may not do is in the NOTICE file and in LICENSING.md; those summaries are NOT
part of this License, and the text below controls.


