1. Definitions
--------------

1.1. "Contributor"
    means each individual or legal entity that creates, contributes to
    the creation of, or owns Covered Software.

1.2. "Contributor Version"
    means the combination of the Contributions of others (if any) used
    by a Contributor and that particular Contributor's Contribution.

1.3. "Contribution"
    means Covered Software of a particular Contributor.

1.4. "Covered Software"
    means Source Code Form to which the initial Contributor has attached
    the notice in Exhibit A, the Executable Form of such Source Code
    Form, and Modifications of such Source Code Form, in each case
    including portions thereof.

1.5. [Reserved.]

1.6. "Executable Form"
    means any form of the work other than Source Code Form.

1.7. "Larger Work"
    means a work that combines Covered Software with other material, in
    a separate file or files, that is not Covered Software.

1.8. "License"
    means this document.

1.9. "Licensable"
    means having the right to grant, to the maximum extent possible,
    whether at the time of the initial grant or subsequently, any and
    all of the rights conveyed by this License.

1.10. "Modifications"
    means any of the following:

    (a) any file in Source Code Form that results from an addition to,
        deletion from, or modification of the contents of Covered
        Software; or

    (b) any new file in Source Code Form that contains any Covered
        Software.

1.11. "Patent Claims" of a Contributor
    means any patent claim(s), including without limitation, method,
    process, and apparatus claims, in any patent Licensable by such
    Contributor that would be infringed, but for the grant of the
    License, by the making, using, selling, offering for sale, having
    made, import, or transfer of either its Contributions or its
    Contributor Version.

1.12. [Reserved.]

1.13. "Source Code Form"
    means the form of the work preferred for making modifications.

1.14. "You" (or "Your")
    means an individual or a legal entity exercising rights under this
    License. For legal entities, "You" includes any entity that
    controls, is controlled by, or is under common control with You. For
    purposes of this definition, "control" means (a) the power, direct
    or indirect, to cause the direction or management of such entity,
    whether by contract or otherwise, or (b) ownership of more than
    fifty percent (50%) of the outstanding shares or beneficial
    ownership of such entity.

1.15. "Sell"
    means practising any or all of the rights granted under Section 2.1
    to provide to a third party, for a fee or other consideration, a
    product or service whose value derives, entirely or substantially,
    from the functionality of the Covered Software. Without limitation,
    "Sell" includes: distributing the Covered Software or a Modification
    for a fee; charging a third party for access to the Covered Software
    or for a hosted or managed instance of it; and incorporating the
    Covered Software or a Modification into a product or service that is
    licensed, sold, or subscribed to for a fee and whose value derives,
    entirely or substantially, from that functionality. "Sell" does NOT
    include using the Covered Software as an internal tool to produce a
    deliverable - such as an engineering study, drawing, model, dataset,
    or report - for a client or employer, where that deliverable, and
    not the Covered Software or access to it, is what is paid for.

1.16. "Deploy"
    means to run, host, or otherwise make the functionality of Covered
    Software available to any user, including over a network or as part
    of a product or service, whether or not the Covered Software has
    been modified and whether or not a copy is distributed.

1.17. "Attribution Mark"
    means (a) the text "Powered by Beamstack"; and (b) the Beamstack
    name and logo in the form published at https://beam-stack.com.

1.18. "Notice Files"
    means the files named LICENSE, NOTICE, and THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES
    (with any file extension) distributed with the Covered Software, and
    any file they incorporate by reference.

1.19. "Network Deployment"
    means a Deploy (Section 1.16) in which one or more users other than
    You interact with the functionality of the Covered Software
    remotely. It includes interaction through a user interface, an
    application programming interface, an automated agent, or any other
    means; and it includes making the Covered Software, or any part of
    it, available so that it is transmitted to and executed, in whole or
    in part, within those users' web browsers or other client software.

1.20. "Corresponding Source"
    of a given version of the Covered Software means the Source Code Form
    of that exact version, including every Modification You have made to
    files that are Covered Software, together with the scripts,
    configuration, build and packaging definitions, and
    interface-definition files that a recipient of ordinary skill needs
    in order to build, install, and run that version from the Source
    Code Form. Corresponding Source does NOT include: (a) files in a
    Larger Work (Section 1.7) that are not themselves Covered Software;
    (b) plugins, extensions, add-on modules, data-defined definitions,
    format codecs, themes, templates, or scripts that interoperate with
    the Covered Software through a documented extension interface and are
    not derived from files that are Covered Software; or (c) generally
    available system libraries, language runtimes, and development tools.

