3.7. Attribution

If You Distribute or Deploy the Covered Software or any Modification, You
must give attribution to Beamstack as follows:

(a) Preserve notices. Keep every copyright, license, and trademark
    notice in the Source Code Form intact, and include the Notice Files
    (Section 1.18), unmodified, with every distribution in Source Code
    Form or Executable Form.

(b) User interface. If the application, website, service, or other work
    through which You Distribute or Deploy the Covered Software presents
    a user interface, that interface must display the Attribution Mark -
    the text "Powered by Beamstack" or the Beamstack logo - such that it
    is:
      (i)   legible, and not materially smaller or less prominent than
            other third-party credits shown in the same place;
      (ii)  located where a user would reasonably look for credits or
            legal information - for example an "About", "Credits",
            "Legal", or "Acknowledgements" screen, a persistent
            application footer, a start-up or splash screen, or an
            equivalent page in the work's documentation; it need not
            appear on every screen; and
      (iii) where the medium supports hyperlinks, linked to
            https://beam-stack.com.
    A work that genuinely presents no user interface (for example a
    software library or a command-line-only tool) satisfies this
    paragraph (b) by complying with paragraphs (a), (c), and (d).

(c) Documentation. Any README, "about" page, product description, or
    academic or technical publication that describes the Distributed or
    Deployed work must state that the work is "based on Beamstack
    software" or "Powered by Beamstack", and must include a reference or
    hyperlink to https://beam-stack.com.

(d) Package metadata. Where the work is published through a package
    registry or ships package metadata (for example a "license" field in
    package.json, or Python package metadata), that metadata must
    identify this License as "LicenseRef-BCL-1.1" (or, for Covered
    Software that carries the Exhibit C notice, "LicenseRef-BCL-1.1-
    Network") or as "Beamstack Community License 1.1", and must not
    represent the Covered Software as being under a different license.

(e) Scope of trademark permission. Paragraphs (b), (c), and (d) grant
    You a limited, non-exclusive permission to use the Attribution Mark
    solely to the extent required to comply with this Section 3.7. This
    License grants no other right to use the Beamstack name, the
    Beamstack logo, or the names of Beamstack projects. You may not: use
    "Beamstack" or a confusingly similar term as, or as part of, the
    name of Your own product, service, or organisation; use the
    Attribution Mark in a way that states or implies that Beamstack
    endorses, sponsors, or is affiliated with Your work; or alter the
    Beamstack logo. Accurate statements that Your work is "based on" or
    "compatible with" Beamstack software remain permitted.

(f) Relief. Beamstack may grant a written waiver or variation of this
    Section 3.7; see "FUTURE AND COMMERCIAL LICENSING" above.

3.8. Network Use

3.8.1. Activation. This Section imposes obligations only if the initial
Contributor has attached the notice described in Exhibit C to the Covered
Software. If Exhibit C is not attached, this Section imposes no obligation, and
carrying out a Network Deployment of the Covered Software is not, by itself,
distribution of it or a breach of this License.

3.8.2. Offer of Corresponding Source. Where Exhibit C is attached: if You carry
out a Network Deployment of the Covered Software or any Modification, You must
offer every user who so interacts with it, at no charge and under this License,
the Corresponding Source of the version You have deployed. The offer must be
made prominently and by a customary means of facilitating the copying of
software - for example, a clearly labelled link shown in the running user
interface and, where the deployment is reachable through an application
programming interface or by an automated agent, a documented endpoint or
response field by which such a consumer can obtain the same Corresponding
Source.

3.8.3. Client-side execution and means of access. For the avoidance of doubt, a
Network Deployment includes making the Covered Software, or any part of it,
available so that it is transmitted to and executed, in whole or in part,
within a user's web browser or other client software; and interaction "over a
network" includes interaction through a user interface, an application
programming interface, an automated agent, or any other means.

3.8.4. Modification trigger. This Section is triggered only by Your
Modifications. If the version You deploy is identical to a version the Licensor
makes publicly available in Source Code Form, directing users to that public
source satisfies Section 3.8.2.

3.8.5. Scope. The obligation of this Section reaches the Covered Software and
Your Modifications to it. Consistent with Section 3.3 and the definition of
Corresponding Source (Section 1.20), it does not reach separately-authored
files, plugins, extensions, data-defined definitions, format codecs, themes,
templates, or scripts that are not themselves Covered Software.

3.8.6. No substitute for other terms. Compliance with this Section neither
grants a right withheld by Section 3.6 nor discharges Section 3.7, and the
obligation of this Section is not satisfied, reduced, or avoided by the payment
of any fee.

4. Inability to Comply Due to Statute or Regulation
---------------------------------------------------

If it is impossible for You to comply with any of the terms of this
License with respect to some or all of the Covered Software due to
statute, judicial order, or regulation then You must: (a) comply with
the terms of this License to the maximum extent possible; and (b)
describe the limitations and the code they affect. Such description must
be placed in a text file included with all distributions of the Covered
Software under this License. Except to the extent prohibited by statute
or regulation, such description must be sufficiently detailed for a
recipient of ordinary skill to be able to understand it.

5. Termination
--------------

5.1. The rights granted under this License will terminate automatically
if You fail to comply with any of its terms. However, if You become
compliant, then the rights granted under this License from a particular
Contributor are reinstated (a) provisionally, unless and until such
Contributor explicitly and finally terminates Your grants, and (b) on an
ongoing basis, if such Contributor fails to notify You of the
non-compliance by some reasonable means prior to 60 days after You have
come back into compliance. Moreover, Your grants from a particular
Contributor are reinstated on an ongoing basis if such Contributor
notifies You of the non-compliance by some reasonable means, this is the
first time You have received notice of non-compliance with this License
from such Contributor, and You become compliant prior to 30 days after
Your receipt of the notice.

5.2. If You initiate litigation against any entity by asserting a patent
infringement claim (excluding declaratory judgment actions,
counter-claims, and cross-claims) alleging that a Contributor Version
directly or indirectly infringes any patent, then the rights granted to
You by any and all Contributors for the Covered Software under Section
2.1 of this License shall terminate.

5.3. In the event of termination under Sections 5.1 or 5.2 above, all
end user license agreements (excluding distributors and resellers) which
have been validly granted by You or Your distributors under this License
prior to termination shall survive termination.

